# Munich Expo Hackathon — .gitignore
#
# Stack is Python 3.12 only (design/decisions/ADR-0002-stack-selection.md, Accepted).
# There is deliberately no node/npm section: adding one needs a new ADR, not an ignore rule.
#
# IMPORTANT — the agent-bus protocol (AGENTS.md) expects test fixtures under tests/ to stay
# trackable, and lanes are tested against checked-in fixtures rather than downloads. `git add`
# silently skips ignored files, so a fixture that only exists on disk passes locally and fails in
# CI. The data-file patterns below are paired with the `!tests/**` negation guard at the bottom of
# this file; anything similar added later must stay above that guard. After adding a fixture,
# verify with `git check-ignore -v <path>` — do not assume.

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor/IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Env / secrets — never commit real credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generic working/scratch areas (directory-level whitelist: keep the dir's own README/.gitignore
# tracked, ignore everything else placed inside it)
logs/*
!logs/README.md
!logs/.gitignore
scratch/*
!scratch/.gitignore

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Downloaded + generated datasets and trained models. Every one of these is reproducible from
# `src.data.fetch` + a seed (contracts/CONVENTIONS.md); none of it belongs in git. Note the
# !tests/** guard below keeps checked-in fixtures under tests/ trackable regardless.
# NOTE the leading slash: root-anchored, or it would also swallow the `src/data/` LANE.
/data/
*.parquet
*.feather
*.joblib

# --- Safety-net negation guard for tests/ fixtures ---
# Whatever gets ignored above (or added above in the future), never let it swallow anything under
# tests/. This now guards real patterns (data/, *.parquet), so keep it last.
!tests/**

# ...except build artifacts, which the guard above would otherwise re-include. Last rule wins in
# git, so these two must stay BELOW `!tests/**`, and any new fixture-guard must stay above them.
tests/**/__pycache__/
tests/**/*.py[cod]
